<section class="how">
    <h2>How to Calculate PayPal Transaction Fees</h2>
    <p>Processing payments through PayPal involves merchant percentage rates plus fixed fees per transaction. Under PayPal's current US standard pricing structure, commercial transactions incur a rate of 3.49% plus a $0.49 fixed fee per invoice.</p>
    <p>Using this calculator is simple: enter your invoice or transaction amount and select your processing category. Our tool instantly determines your exact net payout and also works backward to specify the precise gross billing amount needed to clear your target net earnings after fees.</p>
</section>

<section class="formula">
    <h2>The PayPal Fee Equations</h2>
    <p>To calculate what you will receive (Standard payout math):</p>
    <p><code>Net Payout = Charge Amount - (Charge Amount x Rate Percentage) - Fixed Fee</code></p>
    <p>For example, at 3.49% + $0.49 on a <strong>$100.00</strong> transaction: <code>($100.00 x 0.0349) + $0.49 = $3.98</code> total fee. Your net payout is <strong>$96.02</strong>.</p>
    <p>To calculate what you must invoice (Reverse charge math):</p>
    <p><code>Gross Invoice = (Target Payout + Fixed Fee) / (1 - Rate Percentage)</code></p>
    <p>For example, if you want to clear exactly <strong>$100.00</strong> net after a 3.49% + $0.49 fee: <code>($100.00 + $0.49) / (1 - 0.0349) = $100.49 / 0.9651 = $104.12</code>. You must charge <strong>$104.12</strong>.</p>
</section>

