<section class="faq">
    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    
    <h3>How do I avoid paying PayPal transaction fees?</h3>
    <p>While standard commercial transactions incur merchant fees, personal transfers between friends and family using a linked bank account or PayPal balance are completely fee-free within the US. For commercial invoices, businesses frequently use reverse fee calculation to pass processing costs to clients or offer alternative payment options like ACH bank transfers.</p>
    
    <h3>What is the difference between PayPal standard and international rates?</h3>
    <p>International transactions carry an additional 1.50% cross-border processing fee on top of standard commercial rates, raising the percentage fee from 3.49% to 4.99% plus currency-specific fixed charges.</p>
    
    <h3>Are PayPal micropayments cheaper for low dollar sales?</h3>
    <p>Yes. For transactions under $10.00, PayPal offers a micropayments pricing structure (5.00% + $0.05). Because the fixed fee drops from $0.49 to $0.05, micro transactions retain significantly higher net margins on low-priced digital items.</p>

    <h3>How does PayPal pricing compare to Stripe?</h3>
    <p>Standard PayPal online invoicing rates (3.49% + $0.49) are higher than standard Stripe US card processing (2.90% + $0.30). However, PayPal offers brand recognition and embedded wallet convenience that can increase checkout conversion rates.</p>
